From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 18:15:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] RetroPlayer: run-ahead

Shows the client further ahead than it has actually got to, so that input
appears to take effect sooner. RetroArch's feature, and the single biggest
difference in how a game feels to play.

The client is run once for the frame the emulation genuinely advances to, then
again for each frame of run-ahead. Restoring the state saved after the first
run puts the emulation back where it belongs, so it still moves one frame per
tick, but what is seen and heard is that many frames further on.

Audio is taken from the last run rather than the first: the same frames are
re-run every tick, so it is the last ones that form a continuous stream.

Off by default - it costs an extra run of the client per frame of run-ahead
plus a savestate save and load, and a client that cannot serialise cannot do it
at all. Enable in advancedsettings.xml:

    <games><runaheadframes>1</runaheadframes></games>

or per game, from whatever launches it, since what a client can afford varies
game to game and advancedsettings.xml is read once at startup:

    Window(Home).Property(retroplayer.runahead)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
